# mm.shell.fs

The embedded shell's file command pack, over mm.fs: ls, cat, stat, write,
append, rm, mkdir, mv, df, and mounts, each needing the Files capability. It
follows mm.shell.mcu's rules: the pack installs atomically into an existing
registry, handlers keep to the caller's transaction scratch and allocate
nothing, output is assembled before it is offered, and the status codes are
the shell's.

A command's output is bounded by the transaction scratch and the shell's
staged output, so cat and ls page: each prints what fits and, when more
remains, says on the error stream how to ask for the rest -- cat PATH OFFSET,
ls PATH SKIP. mm.fs keeps no list of its mounts, so the binding names the
prefixes the application mounted, which df and mounts report.
